    },
    {
      "note_id": "NOTE-G2-023-002",
      "case_id": "G2-023",
      "note_type": "hospital_course",
      "note_text": "Colonoscopy was performed after resuscitation and showed diverticulosis with stigmata of recent bleeding. Hemostasis was achieved or the lesion was already flat. The source above was assigned only after endoscopy. The admitting problem was bleeding, not that finished source. Warfarin remained held. No transfusion was required. Acid suppression was not started for a colonic source. Hemoglobin nadir was 8.6 g/dL and the pre-discharge value was 8.8 g/dL. Heart rate fell to 78 and blood pressure was 122/70. INR fell to 1.6. No further melena or hematochezia occurred. The patient was eating and hemodynamically stable. The anticoagulation restart decision was still unsigned. Gastroenterology and anticoagulation follow-up were arranged, with a hemoglobin check.",
      "provenance": "cliniproof_episode_generated"
    }
  ],
